<!--
  `leading-[0]` is what keeps the raise from inflating line-height: the inline box has no height to
  push the line box open with, whichever way the glyph is lifted. So the lift is `vertical-align` and
  not `position: relative`, which would make the mark an `offsetParent` and hand AnimatedText's line
  splitter an offset measured from the page instead of from the paragraph, breaking the sentence
  around every superscript. `0.4em` of the mark's own `0.6em` is the same rise as the `top: -0.4em`
  it replaces.
-->
<sup class="align-[0.4em] text-[0.6em] leading-[0]"><slot /></sup>
